> Derive the block construction and the swap count

For a prefix of length k, keep the tail fixed and enumerate its first k−1
positions. Repeat this child enumeration k times, with a single swap between
blocks. If k is even, completed block i swaps i with k−1; if k is odd, it swaps
0 with k−1. The last block has no trailing swap. Prefixes of length 0 or 1 emit
once.

The correctness induction uses distinct positional labels, even when their
visible values coincide. A child block emits every ordering of its prefix. The
parity rule ensures each of the k labels occupies the last prefix position for
exactly one block. One can check that invariant by composing child endpoint
permutations: an odd child length ends by exchanging its first and last
positions, while an even child length ends in a single cycle on its positions.
For even parent k, successive partners 0 through k−2 bring distinct labels to
its last position; for odd parent k, the child's cycle and the fixed
first-to-last exchange do so. Blocks with different last labels are disjoint,
and induction covers all k! positional orderings.

Let E(k) count emissions and S(k) count swaps. The recursion gives

$$E(0)=E(1)=1,\quad E(k)=kE(k-1)=k!,\qquad
S(0)=S(1)=0,\quad S(k)=kS(k-1)+(k-1)=k!-1.$$
\alttext(Each prefix creates k child blocks and k minus one inter-block swaps, giving exactly factorial emissions and factorial minus one swaps.)

For distinct values, every consecutive row is different. At least one
transposition is needed to move to a different row in a swap-based generation
schedule, so k!−1 swaps is minimal for that schedule model. This is an
element-movement claim, not a lower bound on runtime for every possible encoding
or output interface. Swaps need not involve adjacent positions.

> Retain all 24 original permutations

The original input is 1, 2, 3, 4. The table prints its full legacy order. The
figure tracks where each distinct value sits as row index increases downward.
Its points come from actual retained rows, and the table's swap metadata comes
directly from the same producing execution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heap_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::heap_permutations_trace({1, 2, 3, 4});
    std::print("| row index | values | incoming swap | producing prefix |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.run.permutations.size(); ++j) {
        const auto &v = t.run.permutations[j];
        const auto swap =
            j ? std::format("{},{}", t.swaps[j - 1].left, t.swaps[j - 1].right)
            : "initial";
        std::print("| {} | {}{}{}{} | {} | {} |\n", j, v[0], v[1], v[2], v[3],
                   swap, j ? t.swaps[j - 1].prefix_size : 0);
    }
    std::print("\nOriginal rows {}; producing swaps {}; even-prefix swaps {}; odd-prefix swaps {}; actual " "copied values {}.\n",
               t.run.permutations.size(), t.run.work.swaps,
               t.run.work.even_swaps, t.run.work.odd_swaps,
               t.run.work.copied_values);
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> palette{{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38},
                                                 {22, 163, 74}, {202, 138, 4}};
    for (int value = 1; value <= 4; ++value) {
        std::vector<double> x, y;
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.run.permutations.size(); ++j)
            for (std::size_t pos = 0; pos < 4; ++pos)
                if (t.run.permutations[j][pos] == value) {
                    x.push_back(pos);
        y.push_back(-double(j));
                }
                plot.points(x, y, std::to_string(value), palette[value - 1], 9.);
    }
    plot.title("Original four values: all 24 rows in Heap order").x_label(
        "zero-based position").y_label("negative zero-based row index").x_limits(-.5, 3.5).y_limits(-25, 6).save_svg("build/heap_original.svg");
    if (t.run.permutations.size() != 24 || t.swaps.size() != 23)
        throw std::runtime_error("original counts");
}
