> Measure copying separately from the swap schedule

The API returns vectors containing complete rows. Each emission copies n
integers, so it writes n·n! output values, in addition to n! row objects and
their allocation costs. The recursion's number C(n) of actual calls satisfies

$$C(0)=C(1)=1,\qquad C(n)=1+nC(n-1),\qquad
\frac{C(n)}{n!}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac1{j!}<e-1\quad(n\ge1).$$
\alttext(Recursive calls are bounded by a constant times factorial output count; full-row copying introduces the additional factor n.)

Thus selected generation control and swaps are O(n!), but this materializing
implementation takes O(n·n!+n!) total output work and storage, plus O(n) working
array and recursion for n≥1. This corrects the old unqualified O(n!) runtime
description. It is not a streaming callback interface.

The next block executes each complete size from 0 through 8, once per size, and
compares actual work with independently computed checked recurrence counts. The
plot uses logarithms of positive counts; n=0 output-value copying is zero and is
printed but omitted from that log curve. There are no timing claims.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/heap_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> n, rows, copies, calls;
    std::print("| n | rows | swaps | recursive calls | output integer copies |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n");
    for (int k = 0; k <= 8; ++k) {
        std::vector<int> input(k);
        std::iota(input.begin(), input.end(), 1);
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::heap_permutations_run(input);
        const auto expected = dm::algorithms::heap_permutation_size(k);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", k, r.work.emissions,
                   r.work.swaps, r.work.recursive_calls, r.work.copied_values);
        if (r.work.emissions != expected.permutations ||
            r.work.swaps + 1 != expected.permutations ||
            r.work.recursive_calls != expected.recursive_calls ||
            r.work.copied_values != expected.copied_values)
            throw std::runtime_error("work recurrence");
        if (k) {
            n.push_back(k);
            rows.push_back(std::log2(double(r.work.emissions)));
            copies.push_back(std::log2(double(r.work.copied_values)));
            calls.push_back(std::log2(double(r.work.recursive_calls)));
        }
    }
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.line(n, rows, "rows", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(n, calls,
                                                       "recursive calls",
                                                       {22, 163, 74}, 2.).line(
        n, copies, "output integer copies", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).title(
        "Materializing full rows adds n copies per emission").x_label(
        "input positions n").y_label("log2 selected actual count").y_limits(
        0, 24).save_svg("build/heap_work.svg");
}
